Subclasses of ``ParameterBase`` that forward ``**kwargs`` on to their super
class now carry a ``ty: ignore[invalid-argument-type]``. ty does not recognise a
TypedDict that is generic over more than one type variable as a mapping when one
of those type variables has a PEP 696 default, so it rejects re-expanding the
kwargs with ``**``. The reason is documented on ``ParameterBaseKWArgs``.
